sycl: fuse the MoE weighted expert reduction

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0022.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

A port of the CUDA fusion of #25952. After the down projection a MoE layer
multiplies each expert's output by its weight scale and router weight,
then sums the used experts through one view and one add per expert: for
Inkling's 8 experts, 2 MULs, 8 views and 7 ADDs, 9 kernels per layer pass.
They now run as one kernel, one work-item per output value, in the order of
the unfused muls and adds. The matcher is CUDA's; graph_optimize keeps the
inputs allocated until the fused node, and the memory-range check declines
an output that overlaps an input. Other MoE models with up to 15 used
experts take it too. test-backend-ops covers it as MOE_REDUCE.

